@article{ WOS:001667167400001,
Author = {Malec, Magdalena Maria},
Title = {HOW TO RECONCILE THE NEEDS OF DOGS AND THEIR OWNERS WITH THE DEVELOPMENT
   OF URBAN SPACE},
Journal = {ACTA SCIENTIARUM POLONORUM-FORMATIO CIRCUMIECTUS},
Year = {2025},
Volume = {24},
Number = {4},
Pages = {5-22},
Abstract = {Aim of the study The aim of the study was to assess the attitudes of
   residents of Krak \& oacute;w towards the subject of dog parks, and to
   attempt establish standards of equipment for these sites in order to
   make them both physically and behaviourally safe for dogs. The following
   exploratory questions were posed in the study: Do Krak \& oacute;w
   residents use dog parks, and how often? Do they consider their number
   and equipment to be adequate? What infrastructure is lacking in dog
   parks? Material and methods For the purposes of the study, a survey was
   conducted to assess the need for the creation of dog parks in Krak \&
   oacute;w, and to examine the expectations of dog owners using such
   parks, regarding the infrastructure thereof. The survey was anonymous,
   and it was made available online to users of popular groups on social
   media. Results and conclusions An analysis of dog parks in Krak \&
   oacute;w revealed that the level and degree of their development, their
   technical condition, as well as their locations are highly varied. The
   parks in question include both fenced areas and those with
   infrastructure for people and dogs alike. Furthermore, the number of dog
   parks in Poland is growing, making it difficult to find generalized
   guidelines and content regarding their location and design. The study
   found that most respondents believe that more dog parks should be
   created in Krak \& oacute;w, ensuring easy and equal access throughout
   the city. An analysis of the distribution of dog parks revealed that
   such facilities are missing in many parts of the city. Observations
   conducted at dog parks in Krak \& oacute;w revealed that they are highly
   varied in terms of technical condition, layout, location, and size.},
